%U A398611 6,4,5,5,6,4,3,0,6,9,4,9,0,8,9,6,8,6,0,4,0,7
%N A398611 Decimal expansion of the surface area of a canonical (dual-uniform) 9-gonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398611 The 9-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 9-gonal antiprism.
%H A398611 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398611/b398611.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 3..10000</a>
%H A398611 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Enneagonal_antitegum">Enneagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398611 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398611 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_06">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 6</a>.
%F A398611 Equals (9/4)*sqrt(1 + 4*c - 2*cos(2*Pi/9))*csc(Pi/18)^2, where c = cos(Pi/9) = A019879.
%F A398611 Equals the largest real root of x^6 - 17982*x^4 + 295245*x^2 + 9034497.
%e A398611 134.03558499508778773666270977200802185376658397518...
%t A398611 First[RealDigits[Root[#^6 - 17982*#^4 + 295245*#^2 + 9034497 &, 4], 10, 100]]
%t A398611 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398611 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 9}, "SurfaceArea"], 10, 100]]
%Y A398611 Cf. A398610 (volume), A398612 (inradius), A398613 (midradius), A398614 (height).
%Y A398611 Cf. A398615 (long edge).
%Y A398611 Cf. A398616 (small face angle), A398617 (large face angle), A398618 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398611 Cf. A395165 (surface area of the dual).
%Y A398611 Cf. A019879.
%K A398611 nonn,cons,easy
%O A398611 3,2
